108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (Patient record management is a core part of day-to-day healthcare operations, even in smaller clinics, dispensaries, or reception desks where staff handle recurring visits and basic patient histories. Relying on handwritten registers or loosely formatted notes can make finding a specific patient slow and increases the risk of incomplete entries or inconsistent formats. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (A command-line application offers a fast, dependable way to manage structured records when a full web or database stack is not required. Built as a single Java file \(HospitalApp.java\), the Hospital Patient Record System provides an easy-to-use text menu backed by object- oriented classes, input validation, custom search and sorting logic, and plain-text file storage in patients.txt. This makes the program straightforward to compile, run, test, and maintain from any terminal. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
